---
source: crates/vaab-types/tests/errors.rs
expression: "errors(\"let changing total = 0\\n\\\n         let add: to(Int) returns Int = n -> n + total\\n\\\n         let job = start { add(1) }\\n\")"
---
[changing-captured-by-task] Error: `total` can change, so a task cannot use it.
   ╭─[ example.vaab:3:19 ]
   │
 1 │ let changing total = 0
   │              ──┬──  
   │                ╰──── `total` is declared `changing` here
 2 │ let add: to(Int) returns Int = n -> n + total
   │                                         ──┬──  
   │                                           ╰──── `add` reads `total` here
 3 │ let job = start { add(1) }
   │                   ─┬─  
   │                    ╰─── this task uses `add`, which holds on to `total`
   │ 
   │ Help: use `Shared` instead: `let total = Shared.new(...)`, and change it inside the task with `total.update(value -> ...)`
   │ 
   │ Note: a closure keeps the variable it was written beside rather than a copy of it, so sending `add` into a task would send `total` along with it
───╯
